            "\n",
            "The greedy algorithm in \\ours for target matching is critical to the performance. Consider a duplication algorithm where each segment $S_i$ is simply paired with the target $T$, i.e. $T_i = T$. Since the target text is longer than the text segmented by Algorithm \\ref{alg1}, the generated summary of each coarse stage will be longer as well, leading to a lower compression speed and larger $N$. Besides, the duplication of the target will confuse the model, because some source segments will probably be paired with the same target, causing the model to generate duplicated content. Experiments (Table \\ref{tab:ablation}, ``- stage 2'' versus ``- stage 2 \\& tar. seg.'') show that ROUGE scores declines a lot when greedy target segment is replaced by the duplication algorithm .\n",
