            "\\paragraph{Compression Rate} We analyze the change of compression rate across different stages. In \\ours, compression rate $R_i$ is defined as the averaged source length of stage $i$ divided by source length of stage $i-1$. As shown in Table \\ref{tab:emp}, both compression rates in stage 2 and stage 3 of GovReport are around 0.4, this shows that the compression rate of \\ours across different stages are stable, meaning that the number of segments will decrease to around 40\\\n",
